Description: Personal organizer with a classic paper appearance
 Calendar, address book, tasks, notes, anniversaries, and a year planner in
 an interface styled like an open leather ring organizer. Tabs, rings, and
 folded page corners recall classic 1990s PIM applications such as Lotus
 Organizer.
 .
 The program imports and exports appointments (including ICS files from
 Thunderbird and the Mint calendar), contacts (VCF), and every section of
 Lotus Organizer CSV files. It can also import contacts, appointments, and
 tasks directly from local Evolution and Thunderbird data stores. Public
 holidays and school holidays can be retrieved from openholidaysapi.org. An
 optional three-day forecast uses a local address when available; its disclosed
 public-IP location fallback can be disabled.
 Evolution Data Server integration synchronizes appointments and contacts,
 including contact photos, with system online accounts.
 .
 Notes support print and handwriting fonts, three font sizes, black or blue
 ink, rich-text formatting, and optional spell checking. Appointment reminders
 can use notifications, sound, or both. A session service can issue reminders
 while the main program is closed and report missed appointments after login.
 .
 Window size, full-screen state, and the last calendar view are retained.
 Addresses can be used for LibreOffice letters, maps, email, and printing.
 .
 An optional password or PIN protects the organizer and encrypts its data with
 AES-256-GCM and PBKDF2-SHA256. Deleted items first move to a recycle bin.
 .
 Magnolienbaum allows trusted organizers to share selected tasks,
 appointments, contacts, and notes over encrypted local or direct network
 connections. Shared notes can also include images and PDF attachments.
 .
 All data is stored locally below ~/.local/share/magnolie-organizer/. Existing
 Organizer Klassik 1.0 data is imported on first use.
